      "content": "Insulin is used to lower blood sugar levels, not raise them. For low blood sugar, your best course of action is to consume quick-acting carbohydrates like juice, glucose tablets, or a energy bar to raise your sugar levels. Taking a small amount of water or an oral glucose source can also help stabilize your blood sugar quickly. Do not take insulin or any other medication till you have checked your blood sugar levels first, and consider reaching out to a family member or friend for assistance if needed.",
